===== 7. TLS termination on 443 =====

$ kubectl -n app-config get secret campus-tls-cert
NAME              TYPE                DATA   AGE
campus-tls-cert   kubernetes.io/tls   2      12s

$ kubectl -n app-config get secret campus-tls-cert -o jsonpath='type={.type}{"\n"}'
type=kubernetes.io/tls
# the certificate the ingress is serving, read back out of the secret:

$ kubectl -n app-config get secret campus-tls-cert -o jsonpath='{.data.tls\.crt}' | base64 -d | openssl x509 -noout -subject -issuer -dates
subject=CN=campus.local, O=CampusDevOps
issuer=CN=campus.local, O=CampusDevOps
notBefore=Sep 17 20:44:39 2026 GMT
notAfter=Sep 17 20:44:39 2027 GMT
# an HTTPS request through the controller, -k because it is self signed:

$ kubectl -n app-config exec probe -- curl -sk -H 'Host: portal.campus.local' https://10.96.191.177/ || true
YATRI FRONTEND SITE | uri=/
# and with curl from a pod that has it, showing the handshake:

$ kubectl -n app-config exec probe -- curl -sk -v --resolve portal.campus.local:443:10.96.191.177 https://portal.campus.local/ 2>&1 | grep -E 'subject|issuer|SSL connection|HTTP/|^< HTTP' | head -8
* SSL connection using TLSv1.3 / TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 / X25519 / RSASSA-PSS
*  subject: CN=campus.local; O=CampusDevOps
*  issuer: CN=campus.local; O=CampusDevOps
* using HTTP/2
* [HTTP/2] [1] OPENED stream for https://portal.campus.local/
* [HTTP/2] [1] [:method: GET]
* [HTTP/2] [1] [:scheme: https]
* [HTTP/2] [1] [:authority: portal.campus.local]

