===== 9. Hybrid routing over HTTPS (the checks in section 6 redone) =====
# section 6 only ever saw 308 redirects, because this ingress has a tls
# block and ingress-nginx force redirects http to https by default.
# repeating them on 443. note --resolve rather than -H 'Host:': over TLS
# the SNI must match the Host header or nginx answers 400 Bad Request.

$ kubectl -n app-config exec probe -- curl -sk -H 'Host: portal.campus.local' https://10.96.191.177/ | head -3
YATRI FRONTEND SITE | uri=/
# with --resolve, which sets SNI and Host together:

$ kubectl -n app-config exec probe -- curl -sk --resolve portal.campus.local:443:10.96.191.177 https://portal.campus.local/
YATRI FRONTEND SITE | uri=/

$ kubectl -n app-config exec probe -- curl -sk --resolve api.campus.local:443:10.96.191.177 https://api.campus.local/
YATRI FRONTEND SITE | uri=/

$ kubectl -n app-config exec probe -- curl -sk --resolve api.campus.local:443:10.96.191.177 https://api.campus.local/api/
YATRI BACKEND API | uri=/

$ kubectl -n app-config exec probe -- curl -sk --resolve api.campus.local:443:10.96.191.177 https://api.campus.local/api/payments
YATRI BACKEND API | uri=/payments
# and the http redirect itself, with headers:

$ kubectl -n app-config exec probe -- curl -s -o /dev/null -D - -H 'Host: portal.campus.local' http://10.96.191.177/ | head -4
HTTP/1.1 308 Permanent Redirect
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:52:43 GMT
Content-Type: text/html
Content-Length: 164

